            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_enabled">
                <English>Enable TLB Keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_enabled_desc">
                <English>Vehicle keys, locks and their ACE menus. Off hides every TLB Keys action and lets every vehicle start, without unloading the mod.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_replaceAce">
                <English>Replace ACE vehicle locking</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_replaceAce_desc">
                <English>Hides ACE's own lock, unlock and lockpick actions, and takes over ACE's start-of-mission locking and inventory lock. Off shows ACE's actions next to these.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_acceptAceKeys">
                <English>Accept ACE keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_acceptAceKeys_desc">
                <English>ACE's side keys work as blank side keys, and ACE's master key as a master key for every side.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_startState">
                <English>Vehicles without keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_startState_desc">
                <English>What happens to a vehicle the mission left locked but gave no keys. Start unlocked: nobody finds a vehicle no key opens. Keep: the mission's lock stays, and only a master key or a lockpick opens it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_startState_0">
                <English>Start unlocked</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_startState_1">
                <English>Keep the mission's lock</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockInventory">
                <English>Lock the inventory</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockInventory_desc">
                <English>A locked vehicle's cargo cannot be opened from outside by anyone whose keys do not fit.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_ignitionLock">
                <English>Ignition lock</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_ignitionLock_desc">
                <English>A player whose keys do not fit cannot start the engine of a vehicle that has keys, even from the driver's seat. Hotwired vehicles and AI drivers are not affected.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_insideUnlock">
                <English>Lock and unlock from inside</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_insideUnlock_desc">
                <English>Anyone in a seat can lock and unlock the vehicle without a key, like the door handle of a real car.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockTime">
                <English>Lock and unlock time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockTime_desc">
                <English>How long locking or unlocking by hand at the vehicle takes. 0 is instant. From a seat and with a key fob it is always instant.</English>
            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSide">
                <English>Allow: every key of the side</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSide_desc">
                <English>Vehicles can be locked so every blank key of the owner's side opens them. Leave only one way on to force it; with more than one, the first player to lock a vehicle chooses.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSquad">
                <English>Allow: the owner's squad</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSquad_desc">
                <English>Vehicles can be locked so they open for members of the owner's squad carrying a blank key of the side.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowPaired">
                <English>Allow: paired keys only</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowPaired_desc">
                <English>Vehicles can be locked so only keys cut to them open them. The owner's blank key is cut as it is locked, and spare keys are cut from blank ones.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_claimKey">
                <English>Locking a vehicle first needs</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_claimKey_desc">
                <English>What a player must carry to lock a vehicle nobody has locked yet. Locking to paired keys always needs a blank key to cut. A master key always can.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_claimKey_0">
                <English>Nothing</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_claimKey_1">
                <English>A blank key of their side</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_claimWho">
                <English>Who may lock a vehicle first</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_claimWho_desc">
                <English>Who can lock a vehicle nobody has locked yet, and so become its owner. A master key always can.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_claimWho_0">
                <English>Anyone</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_claimWho_1">
                <English>Group leaders</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_claimWho_2">
                <English>Master key holders</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_squadFollowsOwner">
                <English>Squad vehicles open for</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_squadFollowsOwner_desc">
                <English>Which squad a vehicle locked for the squad opens for: the one it was locked for, or whichever squad its owner is in now.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_squadFollowsOwner_0">
                <English>The squad it was locked for</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_squadFollowsOwner_1">
                <English>The owner's current squad</English>
            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_managePerms">
                <English>Who may manage a vehicle</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_managePerms_desc">
                <English>Who, besides master keys, can change who a vehicle opens for, cut keys, change its locks, name it, give it away or release it. It always takes keys that fit. A vehicle without an owner is managed by anyone whose keys fit.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_managePerms_0">
                <English>The owner</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_managePerms_1">
                <English>The owner and the squad leader</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_managePerms_2">
                <English>Anyone whose keys fit</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSpare">
                <English>Allow spare keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowSpare_desc">
                <English>Vehicles can have blank keys cut to them as spares, and keys cut for another vehicle re-cut.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowWipe">
                <English>Allow wiping keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowWipe_desc">
                <English>A cut key can be wiped blank from ACE self-interaction, making it a side key again.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_pairedAsSide">
                <English>Cut keys still open side vehicles</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_pairedAsSide_desc">
                <English>A key cut to a vehicle keeps opening its side's vehicles locked for the side or the squad. Off: cutting a key ties it to the vehicles it was cut for.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowHandOver">
                <English>Allow handing over keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowHandOver_desc">
                <English>An ACE action on other units hands them a key directly.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_ownerTimeout">
                <English>Owner leaves: release after (min)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_ownerTimeout_desc">
                <English>When an owner has been off the server this long, their vehicles lose their owner. The locks stay, and anyone whose keys fit may manage them. 0 keeps owners for the whole mission.</English>
            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_masterEnabled">
                <English>Master keys</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_masterEnabled_desc">
                <English>Master keys open and manage every vehicle of their side, however it is locked. Off: master keys open nothing.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_masterInArsenal">
                <English>Master keys in the ACE Arsenal</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_masterInArsenal_desc">
                <English>Off hides master keys in the ACE Arsenal from everyone but Zeus, so they only come from modules, Zeus or crates. A unit can also leave this on and blacklist them in its own arsenal.</English>
            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowFobs">
                <English>Allow key fobs</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowFobs_desc">
                <English>Key fobs can be programmed to vehicles, open them like a key, and lock and unlock them from a distance.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_fobRange">
                <English>Key fob range (m)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_fobRange_desc">
                <English>How far a key fob reaches.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_fobSound">
                <English>Key fob chirp</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_fobSound_desc">
                <English>Vehicles chirp when locked or unlocked with a key fob: twice to lock, once to unlock.</English>
            </Key>

            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockpickEnabled">
                <English>Vehicle lockpicking</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockpickEnabled_desc">
                <English>Locked vehicles can be picked. A vehicle whose Eden attribute says it cannot be picked, or whose ace_vehiclelock_lockpickStrength is -1, never can.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_useTsp">
                <English>Use TSP Breach's lock pick kits</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_useTsp_desc">
                <English>TSP Breach's lock pick kit and paperclip pick vehicle locks when that mod is loaded. Off: they do not, and players need another kit.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_useTlbiItems">
                <English>Use TLB Interactions' lock pick kits</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_useTlbiItems_desc">
                <English>TLB Interactions' lock pick kit and paperclip pick vehicle locks when that mod is loaded. Off: they do not, and players need another kit. Whether its lockpicking board handles vehicles at all is TLB Interactions' own setting.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockpickTime">
                <English>ACE lockpick time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_lockpickTime_desc">
                <English>How long picking a lock with ACE's lockpick takes, unless the vehicle sets its own ace_vehiclelock_lockpickStrength.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowHotwire">
                <English>Allow hotwiring</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowHotwire_desc">
                <English>A driver whose keys do not fit can hotwire the vehicle they are sitting in. It then starts without a key until someone with a key locks it again.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_hotwireTime">
                <English>Hotwire time (s)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_hotwireTime_desc">
                <English>How long hotwiring takes from the driver's seat.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_hotwire">
                <English>Picked vehicles can be driven</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_hotwire_desc">
                <English>A picked vehicle is hotwired: the ignition lock lets it start until someone with a key locks it again.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_settings_vehicles">
                <English>Vehicle types</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_settings_keybinds">
                <English>Key bindings</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehCars">
                <English>Keys for cars, trucks and MRAPs</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehCars_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehApcs">
                <English>Keys for wheeled APCs</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehApcs_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehTanks">
                <English>Keys for tanks and tracked vehicles</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehTanks_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehHelicopters">
                <English>Keys for helicopters</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehHelicopters_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehPlanes">
                <English>Keys for planes</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehPlanes_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehBoats">
                <English>Keys for boats</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_vehBoats_desc">
                <English>Off: these vehicles have no keys. No TLB Keys menu, no ignition or inventory lock, modules and attributes skip them, and ACE's own lock actions stay on them.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowKeybinds">
                <English>Allow key bindings</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_allowKeybinds_desc">
                <English>Players can lock and unlock vehicles with key bindings instead of the ACE menu: the nearest vehicle their keys open, or with the key in one of three key slots. Players bind them under Controls, Configure Addons, TLB Keys.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_keyRange">
                <English>Key reach (m)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_tlb_keys_core_set_keyRange_desc">
                <English>How far from the side of a vehicle a key works with the key bindings. A key fob programmed to the vehicle reaches the key fob range instead.</English>
            </Key>
        </Container>

